                        // But we are in case (state == 2'b10). We need to handle splatter in all states.
                        // Better to handle splatter as a separate condition at the top of the always block.
                    end else begin
                        // Resume walking in same direction
                        // Determine original direction? We need to remember direction before fall.
                        // The spec says: "resume walking in the same direction as before the fall".
                        // We need to store the direction before falling.
                        // This requires an additional register.
                        // Let's add a reg dir_before_fall.
                        // This is getting complex. Let's re-read spec.
                        // "When the ground reappears (ground=1), the Lemming will resume walking in the same direction as before the fall."
                        // We need to remember the walking direction before the fall.
                        // Let's add a reg walk_dir (0 for left, 1 for right) or just use state encoding.
                        // Currently state 00=left, 01=right.
                        // When we fall, we need to remember if we were left or right.
